# Story: As a terminal planner, I want each container to have at most one open booking, so that two trucks are never sent for the same container. If a container already has a booking that is BOOKED, another booking for it (by anyone, for any slot) is refused with DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING. After the first booking is cancelled the container can be booked again.

@draft
Feature: Container Booking Limitation

Scenario Outline: Booking a Slot for a Valid Container
Given I am a clerk
When I book a gate slot "<slot>" for container "<container>"
Then the outcome is "BOOKED"

Scenario Outline: Refusing Duplicate Active Bookings
Given there are two drivers booked to the same gate slot "<slot>" for container "<container>"
And another driver tries to book that slot again
Then the booking is refused with reason "DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING"

Scenario Outline: Booking a Slot for an Already Booked Container
Given I am a clerk and container "<container>" has a booking that is "BOOKED"
When I try to book a gate slot "<slot>" for container "<container>"
Then the booking is refused with reason "DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING"

Scenario Outline: Cancelling a Booking
Given I have booked a gate slot "<slot>" for container "<container>"
And I cancel my booking
Then my booking is "CANCELLED"

Scenario Outline: Checking In After Cancellation
Given I have cancelled my booking and container "<container>" has a booking that is "BOOKED"
When I try to check in to the same gate slot "<slot>"
Then the outcome is "FORBIDDEN"

Scenario Outline: Checking In with Clerk Assistance
Given there are two drivers booked to the same gate slot "<slot>" for container "<container>"
And another driver tries to check in to the same gate slot
When a clerk checks the truck in
Then the booking is "CHECKED_IN"
And the gate screen shows the booking as checked in

Scenario Outline: Booking a Slot with Limited Capacity
Given there are two drivers booked to the same gate slot "<slot>" for container "<container>"
And another driver tries to book that slot again
When I try to book a gate slot "<slot>" with room for 1 truck
Then the change is refused because "CHANGE_CUTOFF_PASSED"

Scenario Outline: Booking a Slot Too Early
Given there are two drivers booked to the same gate slot "<slot>" for container "<container>"
And another driver tries to book that slot again
When I try to book a gate slot "<slot>" with room for 1 truck starting in "<time>"
Then the check-in is refused because "CHECKIN_TOO_EARLY"

Scenario Outline: Booking a Slot with Available Capacity
Given there are two drivers booked to the same gate slot "<slot>" for container "<container>"
And another driver tries to book that slot again
When I try to book a gate slot "<slot>" with room for 1 truck starting in "<time>"
Then the outcome is "BOOKED"

